update public.moo_versions set body_md = body_md || E'<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> By May</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> SOP 8-01 authority where a MOA is used</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> City Mayor</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Exchange contacts</th>\n<th>EOC Logistics</th>\n<th><p>Exchange 24-hour contacts and test them.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Reachable?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Arrangements</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Contact test record</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before the season</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Test date recorded</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Operate in events</th>\n<th>EOC Logistics</th>\n<th><p>Receive outage status; pass priority requests; record restoration times.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Priority facilities restored first?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Utility reports</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> EOC log entries</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Each operational period</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Times recorded</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> EOC Manager</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Review</th>\n<th>CDRRMO Head with utilities</th>\n<th><p>Review restoration times after events and each year.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Changes needed?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> EOC logs; AAR</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Review record; CAPA entries</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Annually and after events</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Findings tracked</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** PTN-F06 priority list; arrangements or MOAs; contact tests; EOC log entries; review records.\n\n## SOP 8-06 \\| Partner seats on the CDRRMC: CSOs, private sector and academe\n\n**Process owner:** CDRRMO Head as CDRRMC secretariat, with the SP Secretariat. **Purpose:** Keep every partner seat of the CDRRMC filled by an eligible, accredited and active organisation.\n\n**Table 8.22**\n\n*SOP 8-06 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                                                    |\n|---------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Workflow: WF-SOP8-06 (proposed)                                                                              |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | SP accredits CSOs; City Mayor issues the EO constituting the CDRRMC                                          |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | CDRRMO Head                                                                                                  |\n| **Trigger**                     | Expiry of CSO accreditation; a vacant or inactive seat; a CDRRMC recommendation (e.g., Res. No. 10, s. 2024) |\n| **Forms**                       | PTN-F07; Chapter 1 roster annex                                                                              |\n| **IAT v1.7 indicators**         | A1.2 (3, Low); A10.2 (3, Low)                                                                                |\n| **Functional MR links**         | MR-02                                                                                                        |\n| **Policy basis**                | RA 10121 Sec. 11; RA 7160 Secs. 34–36 and DILG rules on CSO accreditation                                    |\n| **Cross-references**            | Chapter 1 (Annex 1-B); SOP 8-01                                                                              |\n\n**Table 8.23**\n\n*SOP 8-06 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 20%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Check seats</th>\n<th>CDRRMC secretariat</th>\n<th><p>Compare the CDRRMC EO with RA 10121 Sec. 11; list vacant, inactive or unaccredited seats.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> All seats filled by eligible organisations?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> EO 2024-032A; attendance</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> PTN-F07 seat review</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Annually</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Attendance in the last year checked</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Invite</th>\n<th>CDRRMO Head</th>\n<th><p>Invite eligible CSOs, private firms and academic institutions to nominate; include sectoral and faith-based groups.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Nominees eligible?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Seat review</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Nominations</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within 30 days</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Open invitation recorded</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC Chair</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Confirm accreditation</th>\n<th>SP Secretariat</th>\n<th><p>Confirm SP accreditation of nominated CSOs.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Accredited?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Nominations</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Accreditation records</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Per SP schedule</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Copies filed</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> SP</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Amend the EO</th>\n<th>City Legal Office; City Mayor</th>\n<th><p>Draft and issue the amending EO.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Issued?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Accredited nominees</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Amending EO</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within 60 days</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Chapter 1 roster annex updated</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> City Mayor</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Orient</th>\n<th>CDRRMO</th>\n<th><p>Orient new members on the CDRRMC''s functions, the Manual and conflict-of-interest rules.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Orientation done?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> EO</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Orientation record</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before the first meeting</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Record filed</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** PTN-F07 seat review; nominations; accreditation records; amending EO; orientation records.\n\n## SOP 8-07 \\| Annual partner forum and pre-season coordination\n\n**Process owner:** CDRRMO Head. **Purpose:** Meet all partners at least once a year before the typhoon season to confirm roles, contacts and commitments, and to learn from the last season.\n\n**Table 8.24**\n\n*SOP 8-07 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                               |\n|---------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Workflow: WF-SOP8-07 (proposed)                                         |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | CDRRMC Chair convenes; no decision binds a partner beyond its agreement |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | CDRRMO Administration and Training                                      |\n| **Trigger**                     | Each year before the typhoon season (proposed: April or May)            |\n| **Forms**                       | PTN-F01; meeting record                                                 |\n| **IAT v1.7 indicators**         | A10.2 (3, Low); B6.6 (1, Medium)                                        |\n| **Functional MR links**         | MR-02; MR-08; MR-16; MR-18                                              |\n| **Policy basis**                | RA 10121 Sec. 12(c); UNDRR Scorecard 6.1.2, 6.1.4                       |\n| **Cross-references**            | SOPs 8-01, 8-05; Chapter 6 SOP 6-12; Chapter 7 SOP 7-08                 |\n\n**Table 8.25**\n\n*SOP 8-07 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 20%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Prepare</th>\n<th>Administration and Training</th>\n<th><p>Prepare the register summary, last season''s AAR findings, contact directory and the season outlook.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Materials complete?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> PTN-F01; AARs</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Forum pack</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Four weeks before</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Pack circulated in advance</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Convene</th>\n<th>CDRRMC Chair</th>\n<th><p>Invite all registered partners, Part C lead offices, barangay representatives, sectoral and faith-based groups.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Key partners confirmed?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Register</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Invitations; attendance</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> On schedule</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Attendance recorded by organisation</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Confirm roles</th>\n<th>CDRRMO Head with partners</th>\n<th><p>Confirm roles, contacts and commitments; update the register and the resource inventory.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Any commitment changed?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Register; LOG-F03</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Updated PTN-F01 and LOG-F03</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> During the forum</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Changes dated</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Learn</th>\n<th>Facilitator</th>\n<th><p>Review what worked with partners last season and agree improvements.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Improvements agreed?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> AAR findings</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Forum record; ME-F08 entries</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> During the forum</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Lessons logged (Chapter 7)</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Follow up</th>\n<th>Administration and Training</th>\n<th><p>Send the forum record; enter actions in the CAPA register.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Actions owned?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Forum record</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> ME-F05 entries</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within 15 days</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Tracked to closure</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** Forum pack; invitations and attendance; updated register and inventory; forum record; lessons and CAPA entries.\n\n## SOP 8-08 \\| Assistance to other LGUs\n\n**Process owner:** CDRRMO Head as CDRRMC secretariat. **Purpose:** Give help to other LGUs through a lawful, documented route that does not weaken the City''s own readiness.\n\n**Table 8.26**\n\n*SOP 8-08 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                                                         |\n|---------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Workflow: WF-SOP8-08 (proposed)                                                                                   |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | CDRRMC recommends; SP authorises; City Mayor approves; funds and procurement under Chapter 6                      |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | CDRRMO Head                                                                                                       |\n| **Trigger**                     | A request from, or a disaster in, another LGU                                                                     |\n| **Forms**                       | PTN-F03 (outbound); FIN forms as Chapter 6 requires                                                               |\n| **IAT v1.7 indicators**         | A10.1 (1, Medium)                                                                                                 |\n| **Functional MR links**         | MR-02                                                                                                             |\n| **Policy basis**                | RA 7160 Sec. 33; RA 10121; JMC 2013-1 and the applicable proclamation or rule on use of the LDRRMF for other LGUs |\n| **Cross-references**            | Chapter 6 (SOPs 6-02, 6-04); SOP 8-02                                                                             |\n\n**Table 8.27**\n\n*SOP 8-08 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 20%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Assess</th>\n<th>CDRRMO Head</th>\n<th><p>Assess the request and the City''s own risk: is any hazard threatening Ormoc in the same period?</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> City readiness kept?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Request; forecasts</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Assessment note</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within 24 hours</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Own stocks not drawn below Chapter 6 levels without a decision</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC Chair</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Confirm the legal basis</th>\n<th>City Legal Office; City Budget Officer</th>\n<th><p>Confirm the fund source and its legal basis (for example, a mutual aid agreement or a proclamation allowing LDRRMF use for other LGUs).</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Lawful source identified?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Assessment note</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Legal and budget advice</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within 48 hours</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Basis cited in the resolution</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> City Administrator</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Recommend and authorise</th>\n<th>CDRRMC; SP</th>\n<th><p>Recommend by CDRRMC resolution; SP authorises.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Authorised?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Advice</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Resolutions</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Special session if needed</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Resolution numbers recorded</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> City Mayor</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Deliver</th>\n<th>Administration and Training; CSWDO; Treasurer</th>\n<th><p>Deliver cash, goods or teams; obtain receipts.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Receipt obtained?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Resolutions</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Transfer and receipt records</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Per agreement</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> COA rules followed (Chapter 6)</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Record</th>\n<th>Administration and Training</th>\n<th><p>Record the assistance in the partner register and the quarterly report.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Recorded?</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>In:</strong> Receipts</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> PTN-F01 entry; FIN-F03 entry</p></th>\n<th><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within 15 days</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Disclosed with the quarterly report</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** Assessment note; legal and budget advice; resolutions; transfer and receipt records; register and report entries.\n\n# 15. Responsibility Assignment (RACI)\n\n"A" is the single proposed process-accountable owner; "R" performs; "C" is consulted; "I" is informed. The RACI allocates work; it does not transfer legal powers.\n\n**Table 8.28**\n\n*RACI for Stakeholder Engagement and Partnerships*\n\n| **Activity**                            | **MY** | **SP** | **CC** | **HD** | **AT** | **RP** | **EOC** | **LG** | **LO** | **PT** | **CA** |\n|-----------------------------------------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|---------|--------|--------|--------|--------|\n| Partner register and agreements         | A      | A      | C      | R      | R      | I      | I       | R      | C      | R      | I      |\n| Inter-LGU mutual aid agreement          | A      | A      | C      | R      | R      | C      | C       | R      | –      | R      | I      |\n| Mutual aid activation                   | A      | I      | I      | R      | C      | –      | R       | –      | –      | R      | I      |\n| Augmentation request and incoming teams | A      | I      | I      | R      | C      | C      | R       | –      | C      | R      | I      |\n| Part C interface agreements and review  | I      | –      | I      | R      | C      | R      | –       | C      | A      | –      | A      |\n| Utility restoration arrangements        | A      | A      | I      | R      | C      | C      | R       | C      | C      | R      | I      |\n| CDRRMC partner seats                    | A      | A      | C      | R      | R      | –      | –       | R      | –      | C      | I      |\n| Annual partner forum                    | I      | I      | A      | R      | R      | C      | C       | –      | C      | C      | I      |\n| Assistance to other LGUs                | A      | A      | C      | R      | R      | –      | –       | C      | C      | –      | I      |\n\n*Note.* MY = City Mayor; SP = Sangguniang Panlungsod; CC = CDRRMC; HD = CDRRMO Head; AT = CDRRMO Administration and Training; RP = CDRRMO Research and Planning; EOC = EOC Manager and staff; LG = City Legal Office; LO = Part C lead offices; PT = partner organisation or LGU; CA = City Administrator. Where a row has two "A" entries, each holds a distinct act: the SP authorises and the Mayor signs; for Part C, each lead office is accountable for its own indicators and the City Administrator approves interface agreements; for the CDRRMC seats, the SP accredits CSOs and the Mayor issues the EO.\n\n# 16. Performance Monitoring, Quality Assurance and Corrective Action\n\n**Table 8.29**\n\n*Performance Measures for Chapter 8*\n\n| **Measure**                                                                                  | **Evidence**                    | **Review owner** |\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------|------------------|\n| Share of DRRM partnerships with a signed, authorised agreement in force                      | PTN-F01; Vault copies           | CDRRMC           |\n| Agreements reviewed in the last 12 months                                                    | PTN-F01 review dates            | CDRRMO Head      |\n| Mutual aid agreements in force with neighbouring LGUs                                        | Signed agreements               | CDRRMC           |\n| Part C lead offices with a signed interface agreement; Interface Index trend                 | PTN-F04; IAT Part C results     | CDRRMC           |\n| Utilities with a restoration-priority arrangement; restoration times for priority facilities | PTN-F06; EOC logs               | CDRRMO Head      |\n| CDRRMC partner seats filled by accredited, active members                                    | PTN-F07; attendance             | CDRRMC           |\n| Annual partner forum held before the season; actions closed                                  | Forum record; ME-F05            | CDRRMO Head      |\n| Augmentation requests acknowledged and fulfilled; time to arrival                            | PTN-F03; MODE resource requests | EOC Manager      |\n\nFindings go to the CAPA register under Chapter 7 (SOP 7-05).\n\n# 17. Implementation, Validation and Institutionalisation Priorities\n\n**Table 8.30**\n\n*Implementation Priorities for Chapter 8*\n\n| **No.** | **Action**                                                                                                                                                                         | **Office**                                                     | **IAT**      | **When**                       |\n|---------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|--------------|--------------------------------|\n| 1       | Open the partner register (PTN-F01) with all existing agreements; obtain the signed CPR-RIMT MOA; file signed copies of the NRC, OML Center and tertiary-institutions instruments. | Administration and Training                                    | A10.2        | Before the workshop            |\n| 2       | Agree with the Building Official the list of facilities for structural assessment and the rapid pre-impact inspection checklist.                                                   | City Engineer / Building Official; CDRRMO                      | C2.1 (High)  | First quarter 2027             |\n| 3       | Convene the CHO and hospitals on the health anticipatory action plan.                                                                                                              | CHO; hospitals; CDRRMO                                         | C4.1 (High)  | First quarter 2027             |\n| 4       | Propose technical mutual aid agreements to Kananga, Albuera, Merida, Isabel and the Province.                                                                                      | CDRRMO Head                                                    | A10.1        | First quarter 2027             |\n| 5       | Sign interface agreements (PTN-F04) with every Part C lead office; confirm focal persons in MODE.                                                                                  | CDRRMO Research and Planning; lead offices; City Administrator | MR-17        | Within 90 days of adoption     |\n| 6       | Agree restoration-priority arrangements with LEYECO V, NGCP, telecom providers and water services.                                                                                 | CDRRMO Head                                                    | C2.2         | Before the 2027 typhoon season |\n| 7       | Issue the amending EO: City College of Ormoc and an academe seat; third private-sector seat; SP accreditation of CSOs cited.                                                       | CDRRMO; City Legal Office; Mayor                               | A1.2         | First quarter 2027             |\n| 8       | Hold the first annual partner forum, inviting faith-based and sectoral groups.                                                                                                     | CDRRMO Head                                                    | A10.2        | April–May 2027                 |\n| 9       | Platform: add a partner agreements table (type, instrument, term, focal persons, review date) linked to offices and resources; load templates for SOPs 8-01 to 8-08.               | Platform data custodian                                        | MR-02, MR-08 | With the next release          |\n\nValidation: each SOP is reviewed by the offices named in its control block; the mutual aid and augmentation protocols are tested in a joint exercise with at least one neighbouring LGU; agreements are adopted only after City Legal Office review.\n\n# 18. Forms, Registers and Annexes\n\n**Table 8.31**\n\n*Chapter 8 Forms and Registers*\n\n| **Code** | **Form or register**                                                 | **Used in**                 | **MODE**                         |\n|----------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------|----------------------------------|\n| PTN-F01  | Partner register entry                                               | SOPs 8-01, 8-02, 8-07, 8-08 | Proposed; offices table          |\n| PTN-F02  | Partnership proposal and justification                               | SOP 8-01                    | Proposed                         |\n| PTN-F03  | Mutual aid or augmentation request and status (inbound and outbound) | SOPs 8-02, 8-03, 8-08       | Proposed; resource requests      |\n| PTN-F04  | Part C interface agreement                                           | SOP 8-04                    | Proposed; indicator_lead_offices |\n| PTN-F05  | Annual interface review record                                       | SOP 8-04                    | Proposed                         |\n| PTN-F06  | Critical facility restoration-priority list and utility arrangement  | SOP 8-05                    | Proposed                         |\n| PTN-F07  | CDRRMC partner seat review                                           | SOP 8-06                    | Proposed                         |\n\nAnnexes: **8-A** IAT and master requirements traceability; **8-B** model outline of a technical mutual aid agreement; **8-C** model outline of a Part C interface agreement; **8-D** agenda of the annual partner forum.\n\n# 19. Relationship with Other Chapters\n\n**Table 8.32**\n\n*Links Between Chapter 8 and the Other Chapters*\n\n| **Ch.** | **Title**                                                                 | **Link**                                                                                                                    |\n|---------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| 1       | Legal Mandate, DRRM Governance and Institutional Accountability           | Constitutes the CDRRMC whose partner seats SOP 8-06 keeps filled; GOV-05 sends the RA 12287 request to the RDRRMC VIII.     |\n| 2       | CDRRMO Organizational Structure, Staffing and HR Management               | Staffs the partnership functions; holds the EOC facility that C2.1 and C2.2 protect.                                        |\n| 3       | Risk Intelligence, Planning and Institutional Preparedness                | Supplies the scenarios and hazard maps that Part C lead offices use; contingency plans name partner roles.                  |\n| 4       | Early Warning, EOC Activation, Incident Management and Emergency Response | Operates clusters, liaison desks and resource requests; receives mutual aid and incoming teams under ICS.                   |\n| 5       | Recovery, Rehabilitation and Build Back Better                            | Uses partners and the Part C offices in recovery programmes and BBB screening.                                              |\n| 6       | DRRM Financing, Resource Management and Accountability                    | Records partner commitments in the resource inventory; governs supplier agreements, donations and assistance to other LGUs. |\n| 7       | Monitoring, Evaluation, Knowledge Management and Continuous Improvement   | Holds AARs and the CAPA register; records peer learning; governs data sharing with partners.                                |\n| 9       | Public Awareness, Community Resilience and Capacity Development           | Trains volunteers and barangays; runs exercises with partners.                                                              |\n| 10      | Institutional Sustainability, Deep Resilience and Recognition             | Uses the partner register and interface results in recognition and long-term resilience agendas.                            |\n\n# 20. Concluding Notes\n\nOrmoc already has more partners than many cities: national agencies, utilities, a geothermal operator and five CSOs on its Council; a resilience partnership with the NRC and EDC; volunteers under agreement; tertiary institutions in a coordination group; and a record of helping its neighbours. What is missing is the standing arrangement that makes each relationship dependable on the worst night: a signed mutual aid agreement, a restoration-priority list, an interface agreement with each City office that owns part of the risk, and a register that shows which commitments are real.\n\nWriting these procedures does not create the partnerships. Until the partner register holds signed agreements, at least one mutual aid agreement is in force and has been exercised, the Part C lead offices have signed interface agreements, and the first partner forum has been held, this chapter remains a controlled working draft.\n\n# References\n\nThe official text governs.\n\nCity Government of Ormoc. (2023). *Ormoc City disaster risk reduction and management ten-year plan (2023–2032)*.\n\nCity Government of Ormoc. (2026a). *Ormoc CDRRMO–EOC institutional assessment tool* (Version 1.7) \\[Unpublished assessment workbook\\].\n\nCity Government of Ormoc. (2026b). *Ormoc CDRRMO–EOC master requirements traceability and 140-indicator data dictionary* (Version 1.2) \\[Unpublished project reference workbook\\].\n\nCity Government of Ormoc, City Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. (2019–2025). *Resolutions on inter-LGU assistance, volunteers and partnerships* (Res. No. 05, s. 2019; No. 01, s. 2020; Nos. 10, 12–15, s. 2021; Nos. 03–04, s. 2022; Nos. 07 and 10, s. 2024; No. 04, s. 2025).\n\nCity Government of Ormoc, Office of the City Mayor. (2022–2024). *Executive Order on the City CCCM Team (2022); Executive Order Nos. 2023-0025, 2023-0026, 2023-0042 and 2024-032A*.\n\nCity Government of Ormoc, Sangguniang Panlungsod. (2021–2024). *Resolution Nos. 2021-036, 2021-357, 2021-365 to 2021-369, 2023-347 and 2024-102; Ordinance No. 160, s. 2024*.\n\nDepartment of Social Welfare and Development, Department of the Interior and Local Government, Department of Health, & Department of Education. (2021). *Joint Memorandum Circular No. 02, s. 2021*.\n\nNational Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. (2012). *Memorandum Circular No. 4, s. 2012: Implementing guidelines on the use of the Incident Command System*.\n\nNational Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. (2026). *Implementing rules and regulations of Republic Act No. 12287* (signed 14 September 2026).\n\nRepublic Act No. 7160. (1991). *Local Government Code of 1991*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 9418. (2007). *Volunteer Act of 2007*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 10072. (2009). *Philippine Red Cross Act of 2009*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 10121. (2010). *Philippine Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Act of 2010*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 10639. (2014). *Free Mobile Disaster Alerts Act*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 12287. (2025). *Declaration of State of Imminent Disaster Act*.\n\nUnited Nations Office for Disaster Risk Reduction. (2017). *Disaster resilience scorecard for cities: Detailed level assessment*.\n'
